From 10d4f6f4442e2cfdee0689bf876a5bf4f4747e26 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 09:12:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 106/112] signet: require an SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s block signature
 from a height on (-signetslhblock)

A custom signet given -signetslhblock=<pubkey>@<height> requires, from that
height on, an SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s signature by <pubkey> next to the ML-DSA-44
block signature of -signetpqblock (doc/signet-slhblock.md, M4-B of the M4
design, rules 4B-1 to 4B-7). It sits in the coinbase output right before the
witness commitment output, vout[c - 1]: amount 0, a script of exactly 7865
bytes starting 6a 4d b51e "PQH1" 01, then the signature; no other output may
start with the first eight of those bytes. These are compared as bytes at
fixed offsets: the scripts are never parsed, so no GetOp or CheckMinimalPush
runs on them.

The signature signs TaggedHash("SignetSLHBlock", SHA256(challenge) ||
nVersion || hashPrevBlock || slh_merkle || nTime), slh_merkle being the
merkle root with the coinbase the ML-DSA-44 signature covers, its SLH output
cut back to 6a 05 "PQH1" 01, under the context string SIGNET/SLHBLOCK/EXP0.
So the SLH signature is made first and the ML-DSA-44 signature covers it.

It is checked at the end of CheckBlock, after the ML-DSA-44 block signature
and before fChecked, on the same condition (signet_blocks && fCheckPOW), with
the same height (BIP34, an unreadable height counts as reached), the same
genesis exemption and the same per-block verdict below the height with
-debug=validation; the reason is bad-signet-slhblk. Templates are left alone
and Core's template code is not changed: the producer inserts the output.

The option needs -signetchallenge and -signetpqblock at or below its height,
takes one value, and is refused on the Ark-0 signet, on the default signet
and on other chains. A node logs the height and the key's SHA256 at startup.

Nodes without the rule accept these blocks: the rule is a soft fork of the
signet it is given to. On Ark-0 neither the height nor the key is decided:
ARK0_SLH_BLOCK_HEIGHT stays at std::numeric_limits<int>::max() and the key
unset, so the rule is not active there.
